</node>
<node id="最佳解">
  <data key="d0">最佳解</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">种群中适应度最高的食物源。&lt;SEP&gt;在每个特征网格单元中保存的当前最优调度方案，用于生成最终解集。</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2b3dfd7b5cbfa2a90ef71347e70c15cc-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f0490d27025df4a1e3094e5246569dcc-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">An Artificial Bee Colony Algorithm for Coordinated Scheduling of Production Jobs and Flexible Maintenance in Permutation Flowshops-1bbea6e8.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Self-Adaptive_Differential_Evolution-Enhanced_Quality-Diversity_Optimization_for_Distributed_Flexible_Job-Shop_Scheduling_With_Transportation-1158bd89.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1785835930</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="种群">
  <data key="d0">种群</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">种群是进化算法中的核心概念，指由多个个体（候选解）组成的集合，构成进化搜索的基础。在人工蜂群算法等特定范式下，该集合也被描述为所有食物源的集合。在面向多目标优化的进化算法（MOEA）中，种群作为一组解的集合，通过不断更新迭代向帕累托前沿逼近；EMA中通常用P(U)等符号表示由染色体个体组成的种群，并通过选择机制筛选更优个体以构建下一代种群。在诸如HOA‑DSTM的进化框架下，种群中的个体会经历选择、交叉、变异以及局部搜索等操作的迭代优化。种群还常用于计算进化过程的统计特征，例如平均适应度、多样性以及最优适应度，这些适应度特征在双重强化学习（Dual‑RL）方法中被进一步用于构建系统的状态表征。&lt;SEP&gt;算法中所有个体的集合，其规模由种群规模NP决定。&lt;SEP&gt;多个染色体的集合，用于进化算法，种群大小为pop-size。&lt;SEP&gt;算法中所有个体的集合，按适应度值从优到劣排序。&lt;SEP&gt;进化算法中的个体集合，变异算子通过操作增加其多样性，帮助其逃离局部最优。</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2b3dfd7b5cbfa2a90ef71347e70c15cc-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3064a959dca3e0581ecf9bc89a1a99fd-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f0490d27025df4a1e3094e5246569dcc-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e5d47f23ff2115fdf069ba128946a7e2-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-458859b0b2943b04036593edf0f47c6d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c111335adb177428c1a51cb7f78bd2c0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c111335adb177428c1a51cb7f78bd2c0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c111335adb177428c1a51cb7f78bd2c0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e81bd487dda5925119fd6cffd61c849-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b4a2ee09a275fc5e20453805c0167e0d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-49755fa14becf5cd2da17cfb1053b33b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-49755fa14becf5cd2da17cfb1053b33b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">An Artificial Bee Colony Algorithm for Coordinated Scheduling of Production Jobs and Flexible Maintenance in Permutation Flowshops-1bbea6e8.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;A_Feedback_Learning-Based_Memetic_Algorithm_for_Energy-Aware_Distributed_Flexible_Job-Shop_Scheduling_With_Transportation_Constraints-32f047d1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Self-Adaptive_Differential_Evolution-Enhanced_Quality-Diversity_Optimization_for_Distributed_Flexible_Job-Shop_Scheduling_With_Transportation-1158bd89.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;An efficient memetic algorithm for distributed flexible job shop scheduling problem with transfers-316215e1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Scheduling stochastic distributed flexible job shops using an multi-objective evolutionary algorithm with simulation evaluation-1b3e14db.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;A_Hierarchical_Optimization_Algorithm_With_Dual-Cache_Synced_Tuning_Mechanism_for_Distributed_Flexible_Job_Shop_Scheduling_Problem-b3b661fe.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Research on the Flexible Job Shop Scheduling Problem with Job Priorities Considering Transportation Time and Setup Time-efb19039.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-objective optimization for distributed flexible job shop scheduling problem with job priority-91df90f1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;A multi-critical-path co-driven evolutionary algorithm addressing the dual-resource flexible job shop scheduling problem with offline operations and j-8f6b0523.pdf</data>
